 rocking the skull and crossbone  inlays it's a really fantastic guitar  for metal playing and i did a lot of you  know high school shredding on it  but since then you know uh priorities  change and unfortunately yeah i haven't  been giving it the love it deserves  [Music]  now the two oldest instruments in my  collection are from when i was around 11  with my first guitar and this bass which  actually was my older brother's and i  think i just stole it from at some point  both by ibanez or ibanez is probably  pronounced  they are both instruments we got from  our local music store uh when we started  playing so long ago and there they're  the instruments that really kicked off  my brothers and i uh with our musical  you know playing and uh i promised to  never sell that first guitar that i  that one is too sentimental um but it's  yeah it's sitting in my high school  bedroom uh right now it's not a great  guitar but uh i think i'll keep it just  because  it was my first you know and this space  my older brother isn't playing it  anymore so  it's currently my possession and  sometimes i i jam on it i've also used  it for a couple cool gigs that i've got  hired for um the composers of the famous  musical les mis les miserables  they wrote another musical in the 70s  called the french revolution and it  premiered in chicago that was the  american premiere of it and i was lucky  enough to play some base with my twin  brother in it and so this has got some  love  but again mostly unfortunately this sits  in the closet  collecting a whopping amount of dust  so that's it for my personal collection  i do have a bunch of other miscellaneous  instruments percussion instruments brass  instruments things that i've got from  traveling that are on my on my wall just  for fun but i don't really play them  they're more you know for beauty uh then  i have a bunch of other instruments that  i've sold in the past that i used to use  and i'm kind of i'm constantly changing  my collection so maybe one of these days  i'll make another video if i have enough  new and different instruments but for  now thank you so much for watching  please do subscribe if you haven't  already and if you want to support this  channel you can do so by becoming one of  my patrons on patreon and lastly there  is a big discount going on at my online  music school our pajato so if you  haven't signed up yet for lessons and  are interested in lessons on guitar  ukulele bass food whatever we have  teachers for all those and we're  offering a huge 20 discount on your  first four packs so  check that out and i'll see you guys  next time later  [Music]  you

